  "biobricks:reviewed": false,
  "biobricks:reviewNotes": "Determined by the BioBricks licensing-provenance annotation agent (Claude). This brick is an RDF re-serialization of the upstream 'epa-tsca-inventory' brick (declared in .bb/dependencies.txt), whose source is the EPA TSCA Inventory (epa.gov/tsca-inventory). The README states the EPA source is a U.S. government work; EPA data is public domain under 17 U.S.C. \u00a7 105, so classed open / commercial use permitted. Canonical structures are computed locally with RDKit (BSD-licensed toolkit), and any PubChem/CompTox-derived structures are also public domain, so no separately restricting license is introduced. HUMAN REVIEW: note the inventory includes confidential PMN accession records as regulatory entries (identifiers only, no structures) \u2014 confirm no CBI content beyond what EPA already publishes is exposed.",
